# ADR-008

# Capability Registry

Status: Accepted

Date: 2026

---

# Context

RaamaEsha OS is designed as an AI-Native Business Operating System composed of reusable platform capabilities.

The platform must provide a central mechanism through which capabilities can be identified, versioned, discovered, governed, and exposed consistently across business applications, APIs, events, tools, workflows, and AI runtime services.

Integration operations and operation contracts describe capabilities provided by individual organization-owned integrations. They do not provide a complete platform-wide registry of capabilities.

Nandi AI and future Tool Gateway components require a reliable discovery layer without embedding provider-specific or application-specific capability definitions directly into runtime logic.

The architecture therefore requires a central Capability Registry as a platform-level source of capability metadata.

---

# Decision

RaamaEsha OS adopts a centralized Capability Registry as a Platform Core capability.

The Capability Registry is responsible for maintaining the canonical metadata required to identify and discover platform capabilities.

A capability may represent a reusable platform service, API, event capability, tool capability, or other governed platform capability.

The registry will support, as appropriate:

- Capability identity
- Stable capability code
- Human-readable name
- Version information
- Capability category
- Lifecycle status
- API references
- Event references
- Permission references
- Health status
- Extensible non-secret metadata

The Capability Registry is a discovery and governance layer.

It does not execute capabilities.

It does not contain provider-specific business logic.

It does not store plaintext secrets.

It does not replace the Integration Operation Registry.

Integration operations remain responsible for describing operations supported by organization-owned integrations.

Operation contracts remain responsible for defining machine-readable input, output, execution metadata, and runtime hints for those operations.

The Capability Registry may reference or expose capabilities from these platform subsystems through governed relationships established by future migrations.

Nandi AI and future Tool Gateway components may consume the Capability Registry for capability discovery, routing, authorization evaluation, and orchestration.

Actual execution remains the responsibility of the appropriate runtime layer.

---

# Consequences

Benefits include:

- Centralized capability discovery
- Consistent platform-wide capability identity
- Better integration with Nandi AI
- Future Tool Gateway compatibility
- Reusable capability metadata
- Clear separation between discovery and execution
- Improved platform governance
- Easier capability version management
- Reduced coupling between business applications and runtime implementations
- Foundation for future developer SDK and public API capabilities

Trade-offs:

- Additional platform metadata and governance complexity
- Capability lifecycle management must be maintained carefully
- Future subsystems must integrate with the registry consistently
- Versioning and compatibility rules require disciplined governance

---

# Alternatives Considered

## Application-Specific Capability Registries

Rejected because capability discovery would become fragmented across business applications and would prevent consistent platform-wide discovery.

## Integration Operations as the Global Capability Registry

Rejected because integration operations represent organization-owned integration capabilities and are not equivalent to the complete set of RaamaEsha OS platform capabilities.

## Runtime-Only Capability Discovery

Rejected because relying exclusively on runtime implementations would make discovery inconsistent, reduce governance, and tightly couple Nandi AI and future Tool Gateway components to implementation details.

## Static Configuration Files

Rejected because a persistent, queryable, auditable registry is required for a multi-tenant enterprise platform with evolving capabilities.

